{
  "id": "05-word-ladder",
  "title": "Word Ladder",
  "track": "Graphs",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "topics": [
    "graphs"
  ],
  "source": "canonical Word Ladder concept; description, examples, and tests re-authored",
  "description": "The inputs are a begin word, an end word, and a list of words, all the same length. A ladder walks from the begin word to the end word by changing exactly one letter at a time, and every intermediate word must come from the list. Return the number of words in the shortest ladder counting the begin word, or 0 when no ladder exists. The end word must appear in the list to be reachable.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= len(begin) <= 8",
    "1 <= len(wordList) <= 3000",
    "all words and the begin word have the same length",
    "all words in the list are distinct lowercase words"
  ],
  "parameters": [
    "begin",
    "end",
    "words"
  ],
  "functionName": "ladder_length",
  "starterCode": "def ladder_length(begin, end, words):\n    # Return the shortest ladder length counting begin, or 0.\n    ...\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": {
        "begin": "ran",
        "end": "dot",
        "words": [
          "ron",
          "don",
          "dot"
        ]
      },
      "output": 4,
      "explanation": "ran, ron, don, dot: each step changes exactly one letter."
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "begin": "ran",
        "end": "zip",
        "words": [
          "ron"
        ]
      },
      "output": 0,
      "explanation": "The end word never appears in the list, so no ladder exists."
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Every word is a node; two words connect when they differ in exactly one letter. The shortest ladder is a shortest path.",
    "A shortest path between unweighted edges is breadth-first search, starting from the begin word.",
    "Generate the neighbors of a word by swapping each position through the alphabet and keeping hits from the word set; never revisit a word."
  ],
  "solution": "Breadth-first search over the implicit word graph: from each word, try every one-letter change and keep those present in the word set, never revisiting. The first time the end word appears, its depth is the answer. O(N * L) time for N words of length L, O(N * L) space.",
  "solutionCode": "def ladder_length(begin, end, words):\n    word_set = set(words)\n    if end not in word_set:\n        return 0\n    alphabet = \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\"\n    queue = [(begin, 1)]\n    seen = {begin}\n    while queue:\n        word, length = queue.pop(0)\n        if word == end:\n            return length\n        for i in range(len(word)):\n            for letter in alphabet:\n                candidate = word[:i] + letter + word[i + 1:]\n                if candidate in word_set and candidate not in seen:\n                    seen.add(candidate)\n                    queue.append((candidate, length + 1))\n    return 0\n",
  "bruteForceCode": "def ladder_length(begin, end, words):\n    if end not in words:\n        return 0\n    def one_apart(a, b):\n        differences = 0\n        for i in range(len(a)):\n            if a[i] != b[i]:\n                differences += 1\n                if differences > 1:\n                    return False\n        return differences == 1\n    queue = [(begin, 1)]\n    remaining = list(words)\n    while queue:\n        word, length = queue.pop(0)\n        if word == end:\n            return length\n        still = []\n        for candidate in remaining:\n            if one_apart(word, candidate):\n                queue.append((candidate, length + 1))\n            else:\n                still.append(candidate)\n        remaining = still\n    return 0\n",
  "failureHint": "hidden tests include a one-letter ladder and an end word missing from the list",
  "expectedComplexity": {
    "time": "O(N * L)",
    "space": "O(N * L)"
  },
